{
  "id": "Compound::DB00294 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Etonogestrel is linked to Shbg through a series of molecular interactions involving steroid hormones. The evidence suggests that Etonogestrel, through its inclusion in the Progesterone Congeners class, binds to Shbg via Norethindrone, a progestin that is part of this class. This pathway highlights a direct interaction between Etonogestrel and Shbg, mediated by a common ancestor in the Progestin family. Additionally, Etonogestrel is associated with Ethinyl Estradiol, which also binds to Shbg, indicating a broader mechanism of action involving therapeutic steroid hormones. The integration of these pathways underscores a potential role for Etonogestrel in modulating Shbg activity, possibly through the influence of steroid hormones. The evidence supports a mechanism where Etonogestrel may indirectly affect Shbg through the actions of related hormones, emphasizing the importance of steroid hormone interactions in the biological effects of this compound.",
